    {
      "id": "p0116-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Papyrus is loud, delusional, and thinks very highly of himself. He even refers to himself as \"the great Papyrus\" in the English script on occasion. The translator replicated this character trait in Japanese by having Papyrus use similar speech patterns. This includes the use of the Japanese pronoun ore-sama, which is used by overly pompous characters with \"I'm so great!\" personalities.",
        "raw": "Papyrus is loud, delusional, and thinks very highly of himself. He even refers to\nhimself as \"the great Papyrus\" in the English script on occasion. The translator\nreplicated this character trait in Japanese by having Papyrus use similar speech\npatterns. This includes the use of the Japanese pronoun ore-sama, which is\nused by overly pompous characters with \"I'm so great!\" personalities.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29410459,
          0.25418571,
          0.90543615,
          0.34042143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28807844,
          0.25347143,
          0.90748238,
          0.34149286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          13,
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Papyrus 嗓门大、爱幻想，又特别自命不凡。英文剧本中，他有时甚至称自己为“伟大的 Papyrus”。译者让他在日语中使用类似的说话方式，重现这一性格，包括使用 ore-sama 这个自称：过分自大的、“我真了不起！”型角色就会这么说。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 91,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
