    {
      "id": "p0116-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Papyrus always uses the pronoun ore-sama - except in one scene. If the player enters Sans' room, Papyrus will barge in to ask Sans about an action figure. In this one scene, when Papyrus thinks it's safe to be his true self, he refers to himself as boku. This detail adds charm to Papyrus' personality not present in the English line.",
        "raw": "Papyrus always uses the pronoun\nore-sama - except in one scene. If the\nplayer enters Sans' room, Papyrus will\nbarge in to ask Sans about an action\nfigure. In this one scene, when Papyrus\nthinks it's safe to be his true self, he\nrefers to himself as boku. This detail\nadds charm to Papyrus' personality not\npresent in the English line.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.61421675,
          0.35485714,
          0.90582493,
          0.5128
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.6128867,
          0.35414286,
          0.90715498,
          0.51387143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          18,
          21,
          23,
          25,
          26,
          27,
          28,
          29,
          30
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Papyrus 总是自称 ore-sama，唯独一个场景例外。如果玩家进入 Sans 的房间，Papyrus 会闯进来，向 Sans 问起一个可动人偶。在这个场景里，Papyrus 觉得可以放心做真实的自己，便用 boku 自称。这个细节给他增添了英语台词中没有的可爱之处。",
        "status": "draft",
