    {
      "id": "p0116-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Papyrus also has a unique laugh in English: \"nyehehe\". For reasons that are long forgotten, this was finalized as nyahaha in Japanese. It's possible that this was done because \"nyehehe\" can't be transcribed 100% perfectly into Japanese - any transcription would be an approximation at best. Whatever the case may be, Toby approved the choice of Papyrus' Japanese laugh.",
        "raw": "Papyrus also has a unique laugh in English: \"nyehehe\". For reasons that are\nlong forgotten, this was finalized as nyahaha in Japanese. It's possible that this\nwas done because \"nyehehe\" can't be transcribed 100% perfectly into Japanese\n- any transcription would be an approximation at best. Whatever the case may\nbe, Toby approved the choice of Papyrus' Japanese laugh.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29012467,
          0.72994286,
          0.90486321,
          0.81516429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28807844,
          0.72922857,
          0.90748238,
          0.81623571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          49,
          50,
          51,
          52,
          53
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Papyrus 在英语中的笑声也很特别：“nyehehe”。日语最终定成了 nyahaha，当时的理由已经没人记得了。也许是因为“nyehehe”无法用日语百分之百准确地转写，再怎么写也只能近似。不论原因如何，Toby 认可了 Papyrus 日语笑声的这个选择。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
